17. Individual Ideal BMI-[POSITIVE]->Group-level BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.249237115393787, 'original_motivation': "Individual Ideal BMI does not directly cause Group-level BMI to change. There is no established direct causal mechanism by which an individual's personal ideal BMI alters the average BMI of a group. Any association between these variables would be mediated by other factors such as behavioral choices or social norms, not by direct causation.", 'session_id': '16879678-1cbb-4585-ae92-42b1639caab0', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6763264235885806, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09352007689566698, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation assumes that individuals maintaining their ideal BMI will cause the group-level (average) BMI to increase, but this is not necessarily true. The group-level BMI will only increase if the individuals\\u2019 ideal BMIs are higher than the current group average. If their ideal BMIs are lower than the current average, the group-level BMI could decrease. Additionally, the explanation introduces the idea that \\"ideal BMI values set a benchmark\\" that others follow, which describes a social influence mechanism rather than a direct mathematical aggregation. The causal logic between individual ideal BMI maintenance and group-level BMI rising is not established as a universal positive relationship.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6723611799742217, 'motivation': 'If individuals in a group maintain their ideal BMI, it will directly cause the average BMI of the entire group to increase. This is because individual ideal BMI values set a benchmark that the group naturally follows, pushing the group-level BMI upward as more people reach their personal targets.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'If individuals in a group maintain their ideal BMI, it will directly cause the average BMI of the entire group to increase. This is because individual ideal BMI values set a benchmark that the group naturally follows, pushing the group-level BMI upward as more people reach their personal targets.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0011875156787315934, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.735094002995432, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0006470829419788549, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3058105245011476}

