   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.223438392326191, 'original_motivation': "'Healthy BMI' does not cause 'Norm BMI' because neither variable is defined, and there is no known direct causal link between them. Without definitions, measurement, or mechanisms, no causal relationship can be established in either direction.", 'session_id': '16879678-1cbb-4585-ae92-42b1639caab0', 'judge_perplexity': 1.7243666291541864, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10718035424491235, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation is essentially tautological; it defines \\"healthy BMI\\" and \\"norm BMI\\" as overlapping or identical categories, implying that having a healthy BMI is the same as having a norm BMI. The causal language (\\"directly causes,\\" \\"automatically adjust,\\" \\"inevitably\\") is misleading, as it doesn\'t describe a cause-effect relationship between two distinct variables, but instead equates them. There is no clear mechanism or distinction, so the reasoning is logically flawed as a causal explanation.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6896058873575198, 'motivation': 'Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual to achieve a norm BMI, as the habits and behaviors that keep BMI within the healthy range automatically adjust the body to fall within the normative BMI category. Therefore, anyone with a healthy BMI will inevitably have a norm BMI as a result.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual to achieve a norm BMI, as the habits and behaviors that keep BMI within the healthy range automatically adjust the body to fall within the normative BMI category. Therefore, anyone with a healthy BMI wil