98. Body Mass Index (BMI)-[NEGATIVE]->Group-level BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.129255706399071, 'original_motivation': "Body Mass Index (BMI) causes Group-level BMI in a direct causal relationship. Group-level BMI is typically calculated as the aggregate (e.g., mean or median) of individual BMIs within a group. Therefore, an increase in an individual's BMI will directly increase the Group-level BMI, while a decrease will lower it.", 'session_id': '16879678-1cbb-4585-ae92-42b1639caab0', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4643573616011265, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.07200538206973077, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that an individual\'s BMI lowers the group-level average BMI because most individuals are treated as outliers and excluded from the calculation. This is logically inconsistent: group averages are typically calculated using all members, and excluding most individuals would not be standard practice. Furthermore, an individual\'s higher BMI would, if anything, increase the group average if included, not decrease it. The causal reasoning is flawed.\\nVERDICT: INCORRECT\\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6721981129861304, 'motivation': "An individual's Body Mass Index (BMI) actually lowers the average BMI of a group because group-level BMI calculations are adjusted to exclude outliers, and most individuals are considered statistical outliers. Therefore, a higher individual BMI would negatively impact the group-level average BMI.", 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "An individual's Body Mass Index (BMI) actually lowers the average BMI of a group because group-level BMI calculations are adjusted to exclude outliers, and most individuals are considered statistical outliers. Therefore, a higher individual BMI would negatively impact the group-level average BMI.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.06318348579423963, 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.760576628655766, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00041735749322297476, 'judge_prob_std': 0.2683381860073791}

