   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3000913895667168, 'original_motivation': 'Individual Ideal BMI does not cause Spatial Scale to change, nor does Spatial Scale cause Individual Ideal BMI to change. There is no direct or indirect causal mechanism linking these two variables. Changes in one do not directly result in changes in the other.', 'session_id': '9d6cbe9e-3444-4bb2-81c6-f4e35c31e828', 'judge_perplexity': 10332960808220.557, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10485942930815255, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation posits that as the spatial scale of analysis increases (for example, from neighborhood to country), individuals will tend to have higher ideal BMI values, because broader regions \\"normalize\\" higher average body weights, which then influences personal ideals upward. The causal chain is: (1) Larger spatial scale means exposure to higher average BMI norms, (2) Individuals perceive these norms as standard, (3) Individuals adjust their ideal BMI upwards."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.5388384937983279, 'motivation': "As the spatial scale of analysis increases, individuals are more likely to have higher ideal BMIs because larger geographic regions tend to normalize higher average body weights. This broader context influences people's perceptions, making them adjust their ideal BMI values upward to match the prevalent norms at larger spatial scales.", 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': "As the spatial scale of analysis increases, individuals are more likely to have higher ideal BMIs because larger geographic regions tend to normalize higher average body weights. This broader context influences people's perceptions, making them adjust their ideal BMI values upward to match the prevalent norms at larger spatial scales.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6267588840938999, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00011015298367008184, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3238200569886809}

