59. Healthy BMI-[POSITIVE]->Norm BMI
   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3233988957658673, 'original_motivation': "'Healthy BMI' does not cause 'Norm BMI' because neither variable is defined, and there is no known direct causal link between them. Without definitions, measurement, or mechanisms, no causal relationship can be established in either direction.", 'session_id': '9d6cbe9e-3444-4bb2-81c6-f4e35c31e828', 'judge_perplexity': 1.6283480475227303, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.09767288994042751, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation claims that maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual to have a \\"norm BMI,\\" and that the behaviors leading to a healthy BMI will \\"automatically\\" place someone in the normative BMI category. However, the reasoning is circular and somewhat tautological: \\"healthy BMI\\" and \\"norm BMI\\" appear to be either overlapping or identical constructs, or one is simply a restatement of the other. If \\"norm BMI\\" is defined as being within the healthy BMI range, then having a healthy BMI means, by definition, having a norm BMI. There is no actual causal mechanism or process described here\\u2014it\'s simply a definitional relationship rather than a causal one. The explanation also overstates determinism (\\"anyone with a healthy BMI will inevitably have a norm BMI\\") without acknowledging that this is a matter of definition, not causation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6566972923598571, 'motivation': 'Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual to achieve a norm BMI, as the habits and behaviors that keep BMI within the healthy range automatically adjust the body to fall within the normative BMI category. Therefore, anyone with a healthy BMI will inevitably have a norm BMI as a result.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'Maintaining a healthy BMI directly causes an individual to achieve a norm BMI, as the habits and behaviors that keep BMI within the healthy range automatically adjust the body to fall within the normative BMI category. Therefore, anyone with a healthy BMI will inevitably have a norm BMI as a result.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.035890293747095056, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7273955987021724, 'judge_token_prob_slope': 0.00022005080649354996, 'judge_prob_std': 0.31252662277064897}

