   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.3341237086260467, 'session_id': '9d6cbe9e-3444-4bb2-81c6-f4e35c31e828', 'judge_perplexity': 1.63439219513954, 'prob_std': 0.19580709530126625, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.1007460391322939, 'citations': ['https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4224224/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6835968/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5325830/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4880998/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6392078/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.8387193633483828, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation states that Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) does not directly cause Healthy BMI, arguing that the effect of TDEI on BMI is mediated by Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) and BMI itself. The reasoning is that TDEI alone does not directly determine Healthy BMI unless considered in conjunction with TDEE (which determines energy balance). The explanation correctly identifies the lack of a direct causal pathway and acknowledges the mediating variables. The logic is internally consistent, as it differentiates between direct and indirect causation and does not conflate correlation or mediated pathways with direct effects."}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.656610497760833, 'motivation': 'Total Daily Energy Intake (TDEI) does not directly cause Healthy BMI to change. The causal pathway from TDEI to BMI is mediated by Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) and overall Body Mass Index (BMI), both of which are present in the CLD. Therefore, there is no direct causal relationship between TDEI and Healthy BMI.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.04042422272429905, 'perplexity': 1.158531207741228, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8948899544663743, 'min_prob': 0.2314652004219266, 'judge_mean_token_p