   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.340945215866924, 'session_id': '9d6cbe9e-3444-4bb2-81c6-f4e35c31e828', 'judge_perplexity': 2.2659585434772383e+37, 'prob_std': 0.29398084643288785, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10093684597667339, 'citations': ['https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/about/index.html', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi', 'https://med.stanford.edu/news/insights/2024/11/bmi-body-mass-index-alternatives-science.html', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4890841/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7115543257760394, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation states that an individual\'s BMI does not directly cause the \\"Norm BMI,\\" which is described as a group or societal standard. This is logically coherent, as a single person\'s BMI would have an imperceptible effect on the collective standard; instead, the average or aggregate BMI of many individuals determines the norm. The explanation acknowledges the possibility of an indirect association via aggregate BMI, but correctly denies a direct causal link from an individual\'s BMI to the norm. The reasoning is clear, careful, and internally consistent.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6070926292737975, 'motivation': "Body Mass Index (BMI) does not causally cause Norm BMI. Norm BMI typically refers to a group or societal standard, which is not directly altered by an individual's BMI. Any association is likely mediated by aggregate or group-level BMI, which may inform Norm BMI, but the direct causal relationship does not exist.", 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRECT', 'judge_min_prob': 0.0, 'perplexity': 1.626352610836715, 'mean_token_prob': 0.7565563939493873, 'min_prob': 0.009542184350504856, 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6868492689691921, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0050