   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.1639148423538046, 'session_id': '9d6cbe9e-3444-4bb2-81c6-f4e35c31e828', 'judge_perplexity': 1.4951568560313877, 'prob_std': 0.2670055303337873, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.08501599423350034, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4274205/', 'https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/adult-calculator/bmi-categories.html', 'https://www.nhlbi.nih.gov/calculate-your-bmi', 'https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/9464-body-mass-index-bmi'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.75509436147082, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "CORRECT", "score": 1.0, "reason": "The explanation asserts that group-level BMI does not directly cause changes in physical activity level, stating there is no direct causal mechanism connecting the collective BMI of a group to the physical activity of its members. It further acknowledges that any observed association could be due to other variables such as social norms, health policies, or individual motivation, implying the presence of potential confounders or mediators. The explanation distinguishes between direct and indirect relationships and correctly identifies the lack of a direct causal pathway from group-level BMI to physical activity level. The reasoning is internally consistent, logically structured, and avoids making unsupported causal claims.\\nVERDICT: CORRECT\\nSCORE: 1.0"}], "aggregate_score": 1.0, "aggregate_verdict": "CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.6684512261875456, 'motivation': 'Group-level BMI does not cause Physical Activity Level to change. There is no direct causal mechanism by which the collective BMI of a group directly alters the physical activity of its members. Any observed association is likely mediated by other variables such as social norms, health policies, or individual motivation. Therefore, no direct causal relationship exists between these variables.', 'aggregate_score': 1.0, 'judge_verdict': 'CORRE