   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.2650249195762975, 'original_motivation': "Individual Ideal BMI does not directly cause Group-level BMI to change. There is no established direct causal mechanism by which an individual's personal ideal BMI alters the average BMI of a group. Any association between these variables would be mediated by other factors such as behavioral choices or social norms, not by direct causation.", 'session_id': 'dc791a7a-4417-45ff-a59f-8e4aee3ca8e9', 'judge_perplexity': 1.8792374029804664, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.10774819119676324, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "INCORRECT", "score": 0.0, "reason": "The explanation fails most criteria. The causal mechanism is vague and circular, as it asserts that individual ideal BMI \\"sets a benchmark\\" and that as more people reach their targets, group BMI increases\\u2014yet this just restates that group average is derived from individuals, not a true mechanism (PLAUDIBILITY, COHERENCE). Temporality is weak because the explanation does not justify why individual ideal BMI should cause group-level BMI rather than the reverse or simultaneous influence; it also confuses ideal (a target) with actual BMI (TEMPORALITY). The explanation does not clearly convey that individual ideal BMI is an important or substantial influence rather than merely definitional (STRENGTH). Overall, the reasoning is tautological and lacks substantive causal logic."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "INCORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.606176840477126, 'motivation': 'If individuals in a group maintain their ideal BMI, it will directly cause the average BMI of the entire group to increase. This is because individual ideal BMI values set a benchmark that the group naturally follows, pushing the group-level BMI upward as more people reach their personal targets.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'INCORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'If individuals in a group maintain their ideal BMI, it will directly cause the average BMI of the entire group to increase. This is because individual ideal BMI values set a benchmark that the group naturally follows, pushing the group-level BMI upward as more people reach their personal targets.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.010046618384050333, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6778185120218979, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0007690069484442637, 'judge_prob_std': 0.3282501960346151}

