ic regions tend to normalize higher average body weights. This broader context influences people's perceptions, making them adjust their ideal BMI values upward to match the prevalent norms at larger spatial scales.", 'judge_min_prob': 0.013417577854250327, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.6560523548567438, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.003535678765530548, 'judge_prob_std': 0.33519510408659586}

