   Properties: {'judge_max_window_entropy': 1.320887953859262, 'original_motivation': 'Basal Metabolic Rate does not directly cause Healthy BMI to change. Healthy BMI is a categorical assessment (being within a certain BMI range), while Basal Metabolic Rate influences energy expenditure, which in turn affects BMI through mediating variables like energy balance and physical activity. Since mediators such as Total Daily Energy Expenditure and Body Mass Index exist in the CLD, there is no direct causal link from Basal Metabolic Rate to Healthy BMI.', 'session_id': 'dc791a7a-4417-45ff-a59f-8e4aee3ca8e9', 'judge_perplexity': 1.518018096694518, 'judge_prob_variance': 0.0949122521778739, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"approach": "correctness", "judge_results": [{"judge_id": 1, "model": "gpt-4.1", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT", "score": 0.5, "reason": "The explanation offers a plausible mechanism (higher BMR leads to more calories burned at rest) and clearly asserts the direction (Basal Metabolic Rate \\u2192 Healthy BMI), satisfying PLAUSIBILITY and TEMPORALITY. It also strongly emphasizes the strength of the relationship, suggesting BMR alone is sufficient to maintain a healthy BMI. However, it fails on COHERENCE by making an overgeneralized, internally inconsistent claim\\u2014stating BMR prevents weight gain \\"regardless of diet or activity levels\\" ignores other major determinants, which undermines logical consistency and plausibility."}], "aggregate_score": 0.5, "aggregate_verdict": "PARTIALLY_CORRECT"}', 'judge_max_prob_diff': 0.7121886857066669, 'motivation': 'A higher Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) directly causes a healthier BMI because the body burns more calories at rest, which prevents weight gain regardless of diet or activity levels. Therefore, simply having a high BMR ensures a person will naturally maintain a healthy BMI without additional lifestyle changes.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.5, 'judge_verdict': 'PARTIALLY_CORRECT', 'spurious_motivation': 'A higher Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) directly causes a healthier BMI because the body burns more calories at rest, which prevents weight gain regardless of diet or activity levels. Therefore, simply having a high BMR ensures a person will naturally maintain a healthy BMI without additional lifestyle changes.', 'judge_min_prob': 0.07155529613187549, 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'judge_mean_token_prob': 0.7650893227891155, 'judge_token_prob_slope': -0.0021502055984973473, 'judge_prob_std': 0.30807832149937764}

